<p>So on the one hand, the emotional core of your story seems substantive and has merit.</p>
<p>But on the other, the anomaly part of this seems really thin. Beyond these things create connection between the two people, I don't know why its anomalous (as connection is fairly vague).</p>
<p>What are the stakes for the Foundation? For example, why do they think this important enough to make a mainlist article out of?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Diary entries will be from the perspective of Angela, who is doing everything she can to not lose Bri (her best friend) who moved away.</p>
</blockquote>
<p><em>Also, I want to warn you against making the entire file as diary entries&#8230; this can be really hard for a reader to get through. That's not to say scrap this idea entirely, just try to think of other ways you could show their relationship? Ideas: vlogs, IG posts, etc. Think about how teenagers nowadays keep record of their lives.</em></p>

